    },
    "body": "Strict four-bit K2 value projection lost answer accuracy despite a repaired serving-identical hard-choice bridge. This adds a Rust driver that updates only the value producer from ordinary answer loss through the frozen learned H4 composition bank, then independently exports, reloads and compares each candidate with both retained controls.\n\nBoth fixed 640-update fits complete. Learned native answers are 112/113 and 126/128 on the 128-row original/stress panels: 479/512 versus 451 projected and 467 unrestricted-parent answers. Cross-entropy improves on all four panels. All 24 parent gains and 12 losses remain recorded; source/native packet/Q16 traces and answers agree on all 512 rows. The lost rows retain strong correct-source mass, so the evidence does not justify changing address selection.\n\nValidation: two focused release driver tests, release example build, cargo fmt --check, claim-wording gate and diff whitespace check; both actual zero-update check-mode replays; both full fixed fits and independent export/reload. Frozen NoRead/bank numerical files remain byte-identical. Source review and independent artifact/result review are recorded in the evidence receipt. Fit workers took 148.275/124.302 seconds at 512278528/478838784 bytes peak RSS; complete preparation/review/build/fit/evaluation/delivery cost is charged separately.\n\nThese are exposed authored development panels, with additional training versus the controls. No geometric superiority, held-out language, complete native serving or energy claim follows. Wider upstream coefficients and the float tail remain open. The roadmap retains all candidates, ends this dose and advances the next attention coefficient boundary; no selector/scale/alphabet/bank sweep or GroundedSession edits.\n\nReferences #1512, #973.\n",
